#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-contrast.md:0
msgid ""
"Turn on high contrast in Ubuntu Desktop to make windows and buttons easier "
"to see without changing the screen brightness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-contrast.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-contrast.md:11
msgid "Adjust the contrast"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-contrast.md:13
msgid ""
"You can adjust the contrast of windows and buttons so that they’re easier to "
"see. This is not the same as changing the brightness of the whole screen; "
"only parts of the user interface will change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-contrast.md:15
msgid "Open the Activities overview and start typing **accessibility**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-contrast.md:16
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Accessibility` to open the panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-contrast.md:17
msgid "Open the {guilabel}`Seeing` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-contrast.md:18
msgid "Enable the {guilabel}`High Contrast` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/adjust-the-contrast.md:21
msgid ""
"You can turn high contrast on and off by clicking the {ref}`accessibility "
"icon <find-the-accessibility-menu>` on the top bar and selecting {guilabel}"
"`High Contrast`."
msgstr ""
